24:- [ ] **Phase 10: Timestamp Domain Abstraction** - Eliminate scattered time conversion logic, centralize via strongly-typed Timestamp class
25-
26-## Phase Details
27-
28-### Phase 1: Worker Foundation & Binance Spike
29-**Goal**: A single deployed Cloudflare Worker serves the app's static assets and API skeleton, D1 schema is live, and Binance reachability from that Worker is proven safe to build on.
30-**Depends on**: Nothing (first phase)
31-**Requirements**: INFRA-01, INFRA-02, INFRA-03, INFRA-05, DATA-07
32-**Success Criteria** (what must be TRUE):
--
166:### Phase 10: Timestamp Domain Abstraction
167-**Goal**: Eliminate scattered time conversion logic (`Math.floor(ms / 1000)`) across codebase. Replace with strongly-typed `Timestamp` class for type safety and single source of truth.
168-**Depends on**: Phase 9
169-**Requirements**: CODE-01 (type safety), CODE-02 (maintainability)
170-**Success Criteria** (what must be TRUE):
171-  1. All backend time operations use `Timestamp` API instead of `Math.floor(ms / 1000)`.
172-  2. All frontend time operations use `Timestamp` API for conversions.
173-  3. Zero `Math.floor(ms / 1000)` remains in production code.
174-  4. `Timestamp` class fully tested with 44/44 unit tests passing.
